      "note": "The countable choice-free theorem (thm:prop-completeness/compactness, built on an enumeration of Fm_CPL) is distinguished from the BPI-relative arbitrary-language theorem (supplement 37-42; free-boolean 16-23, 262-263, 277-291; 016 body 22-26 and table 247-279). Effective finite-input decision procedures are separated from it: finite-input transfer into Fm_CPL in ZF with answers independent of the renaming, reduction to SAT/TAUT with 2^k rows, no encoding or enumeration of Form(P) for uncountable P, and a proof boundary stating that the BPI theorem yields no procedure (016 body 136-245). Each has a written annex proof (annex 016 13-226), plus a worked example and a failure case (016 body 284-332). All files on route: parts/p02.tex lines 26, 33, 34 (under main.tex:30); annex/p02.tex lines 27-28 (under main.tex:55); parts/p01.tex line 18; annex/p01-route.tex line 3."
